Explain file permissions versus directory permissions when granting a service access to one configuration file.|A teammate belongs to the file group but cannot open a file under a private parent directory. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Describe how you would diagnose a permission denial without broadening access unnecessarily.|A service running as app cannot read a root-owned configuration with mode 600. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain symlink-based releases and how you would make rollback safe.|A deployment symlink points to a release directory that was removed. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the differences between hard links and symlinks during file cleanup.|Removing a filename does not reclaim the expected space and another hard link exists. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how stdout and stderr should be handled in a production shell pipeline.|A command reports errors on the terminal but the downstream parser receives none. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain safe shell handling of filenames containing spaces or wildcard characters.|A cleanup script fails on filenames containing spaces. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Describe how you would safely locate and stop a specific service process.|A saved PID now belongs to a different process than yesterday. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain a graceful shutdown sequence and when forced termination becomes appropriate.|A service needs time to flush buffered work during shutdown. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would investigate a df and du discrepancy.|df shows a full filesystem but du finds much less visible file data. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain an inode exhaustion incident and a lasting prevention measure.|A filesystem has free gigabytes but creating a new file fails with no space. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how to distinguish a descriptor leak from a legitimate capacity requirement.|A service logs too many open files while disk space remains healthy. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain why high load with idle CPU calls for more than a CPU graph.|Load rises sharply while CPU utilization remains low and storage is slow. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would distinguish useful caching from memory pressure.|A host shows low free RAM but high available RAM and no memory pressure. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the difference between a signal-based exit code and evidence of an OOM kill.|A container exits with 137 after a deployment. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how binding addresses affect service reachability.|An application responds locally but not from another host. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Describe how you would investigate inconsistent hostname resolution on Linux.|A name resolves with a DNS tool but the application gets a different address. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain why a read-only filesystem error differs from a permission denial.|Writes fail with read-only filesystem after storage errors. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain why patch verification must include running processes.|A security update replaces a binary but an old process is still running. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain zombie processes and how a service should manage child lifecycles.|A service parent accumulates many zombie children. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would use system-call tracing safely during an incident.|A process hangs while opening a path and logs provide little detail. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Compare scheduling priority with hard resource limits.|A batch job interferes with latency-sensitive work on a shared host. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the risks of treating swap settings as a substitute for capacity planning.|Latency spikes coincide with sustained swap-in and swap-out activity. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain least privilege for a service that needs one privileged operation.|A service only needs to bind a privileged port. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would debug an unexpected effective ACL permission.|An ACL entry grants write but effective permissions show read-only. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain atomic visibility versus durable persistence in a configuration update.|Readers sometimes see partially written configuration files. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain the roles of namespaces and cgroups in container isolation.|Two containers have different interfaces but contend for host CPU. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how resource limits can cause latency on an otherwise idle host.|A service is slow despite idle host cores and rising throttling counters. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Outline a safe response to suspected filesystem corruption.|A volume reports metadata errors while applications continue writing. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain clock choices for deadlines and distributed log timestamps.|A timeout calculation behaves strangely after a clock correction. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would distinguish a shared kernel or device problem from an application bug.|Several applications experience I/O failures after a kernel update. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
